{# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Africa GATES — "We are Africa" band (globe)
   Sits directly after the hero on the homepage. Light band, dashed
   background guides, centred globe, dashed annotation card at its right,
   and the stat card overlapping the sphere's lower edge.

   Requires (see docs/GLOBE-BAND.md):
     <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/globe-band.css">
     <script src="/assets/js/vendor/d3-7.9.0.min.js"></script>
     <script src="/assets/js/vendor/topojson-client-3.1.0.min.js"></script>
     <script src="/assets/js/globe-band.js" defer></script>

   ── EVERY FIGURE ON IT IS COUNTED, NONE IS TYPED ────────────────────────

   The handoff drew this band over sixteen invented cities — Lagos on 41,280
   ballots verified in 1.1 seconds, arcs between "verification nodes", and an
   annotation stating a median latency as a measured fact. This platform has no
   such nodes and records no per-ballot timing; there has never been a column
   for either. `GlobeBand` supplies the markers instead, from the same joins the
   footer's "live in …" sentence uses, so the globe and that sentence cannot
   disagree about which nations are live.

   `globe_countries` is therefore NOT optional-with-a-pretty-fallback. Absent,
   the sphere draws with no markers — which is what a site with no approved
   nominee actually looks like, and what the annotation then says.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
<section class="reg" id="agGlobeBand">
  <div class="reg__guides" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>

  <div class="hw reg__in">
    <div class="reg__hd">
      <h2 class="reg__h">{{ globe_heading|default('We are Africa') }}</h2>
      <p class="reg__sub">One verified index for the continent — <span class="reg__sub-em">close to voters, close to the record.</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="reg__body">
      <div class="reg__stage" id="agGlobeStage"
           data-countries="{{ (globe_countries|default([]))|json_encode|e('html_attr') }}"
           data-topojson="{{ globe_topojson|default('/assets/geo/countries-110m.json') }}">
        <canvas id="agGlobe"></canvas>
        <div class="reg__layer" id="agGlobeNodes"></div>

        {#
          TWO ROWS, NOT THREE. The design's other two were "Verification node"
          — a named city that routes a ballot — and "Median verification", a
          time in seconds. This platform has never had a column for either. A
          row whose value can only be an em dash is worse than an absent row:
          it reads as data that failed to load.

          `GlobeBandTest` sweeps this file for that retired wording, and strips
          Twig comments before it does, so this block may name what it removed.
        #}
        <div class="ccard" id="agGlobeCard" role="dialog" aria-label="Country detail">
          <div class="ccard__hd">
            <div>
              <p class="ccard__nm" data-globe-name>&mdash;</p>
              <p class="ccard__rg" data-globe-code>&mdash;</p>
            </div>
            <button class="ccard__x" type="button" data-globe-close aria-label="Close">✕</button>
          </div>
          <div class="ccard__rows">
            <div class="crow"><span>Nominees standing</span><b data-globe-nominees>&mdash;</b></div>
            <div class="crow"><span>Votes cast</span><b data-globe-votes>&mdash;</b></div>
          </div>
          {# Shown instead of the rows for a nation with nothing in a live award —
             stated, because a card of two zeros looks like a fault. #}
          <p class="ccard__none" data-globe-none hidden>No nominee is standing here in a live award yet.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="reg__note">{{ globe_note|default('Each marker is a nation with a nominee standing in a live award.') }}</aside>
    </div>

    {#
      ── THE FOUR FIGURES ────────────────────────────────────────────────

      This card is the homepage's ONE stat strip. `home.twig` carried a second
      one immediately above the band with the same four cells; the handoff's
      page inventory says delete one, and the duplicate is the one without a
      globe attached to it. Its live/constant logic is kept here whole, because
      that logic is the honest part: real counts once there is activity, and the
      platform's structural constants before that — never a strip of dead zeros.

      Three of the constants are RULES, not literals. `community_pct`/`judge_pct`
      come from `RuleEngine::weights()` and the criteria count from the active
      rubric; CLAUDE.md is explicit that the split "is set per cycle rather than
      fixed forever", and this repo has already shipped four published promises
      that outlived the rule they described, on pages stating a weighting as a
      constant. `0–1,000` stays literal: the index range is structural.
    #}
    {% set _activity = site_stats.total_profiles|default(0) + site_stats.total_votes|default(0) %}
    <div class="reg__cols">
      {% if _activity > 0 %}
        <div class="reg__col"><div class="reg__n" data-countup="{{ site_stats.total_profiles|default(0) }}">{{ site_stats.total_profiles|default(0)|number_format }}</div><div class="reg__l">Verified profiles</div></div>
        <div class="reg__col"><div class="reg__n" data-countup="{{ site_stats.total_votes|default(0) }}">{{ site_stats.total_votes|default(0)|number_format }}</div><div class="reg__l">Votes cast</div></div>
        <div class="reg__col"><div class="reg__n" data-countup="{{ site_stats.nations_live|default(0) }}">{{ site_stats.nations_live|default(0)|number_format }}</div><div class="reg__l">Nation{{ site_stats.nations_live|default(0) == 1 ? '' : 's' }} live</div></div>
        <div class="reg__col"><div class="reg__n" data-countup="{{ site_stats.categories|default(0) }}">{{ site_stats.categories|default(0)|number_format }}</div><div class="reg__l">Award categories</div></div>
      {% else %}
        <div class="reg__col"><div class="reg__n" data-countup="{{ nations_count|default(54) }}">{{ nations_count|default(54) }}</div><div class="reg__l">Nations in scope</div></div>
        <div class="reg__col"><div class="reg__n">0–1,000</div><div class="reg__l">CPI score scale</div></div>
        <div class="reg__col"><div class="reg__n">{{ community_pct|default(45) }}<small>%</small> + {{ judge_pct|default(55) }}<small>%</small></div><div class="reg__l">Public votes + jury</div></div>
        <div class="reg__col"><div class="reg__n" data-countup="{{ jury_criteria|default(4) }}">{{ jury_criteria|default(4) }}</div><div class="reg__l">Jury criteri{{ jury_criteria|default(4) == 1 ? 'on' : 'a' }}</div></div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
